{"kind":"request","text":"Correct the owed-supersessions count for withdrawn successors.\n\nDiscovered while repairing the review basis for task/world-basis. At head 51fb936e23b9e24ab59aee6df11d03a35389ba3e the fold counts every un-retired artifact except the last ever recorded at a path, so where A is live, B follows at the same path, and B is then superseded, it reports one supersession still owed. Nothing is owed: A is the current artifact for that path again, and following the warning would retire it because of a replacement that no longer exists. The same reasoning was reached independently in review report git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:70e122a3f4c6bc33e885685fcd818318bdfbe145, which is cited here as evidence only and not rested on, because that report is stale.\n\nThe rule to implement: a live artifact is owed a supersession only while a live artifact later at the same path stands in its place. The per-artifact row stays as it is, because B really did follow a live A and that is a fact about what happened; what changes is the aggregate that tells a reader what to do.","body":{"branch":"task/world-basis","conditions":"OmittedSupersessions counts a live artifact only while a live later artifact at the same path stands in its place; a regression test pins the withdrawn-successor case with a live-successor positive control; the human page states rows, paths and owed acts without claiming an act is owed when none is; existing succession and unable-to-flare tests keep passing.","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}